+    // SK-NSRESOLVE: a Resolver resolves its host ONCE and replays that result (or that error) to
+    // every later request. Built at daemon start, it froze a start-up DNS failure into a permanent
+    // "code=0" for every name lookup until the process died. Requests now take the resolver through
+    // resolver(), and a request that got no HTTP response at all drops it so the next re-resolves.
+    std::mutex resolverMtx_ {};
